# Virtual threads are a JVM runtime fact, not a language feature: there is no
# spelling for one on the native backend, and the carriers native's own `ctl`
# mechanism runs on are pthreads the runtime owns rather than anything a Dawn
# program can start (docs/oneshot-design.md 11.11). So this question has one
# backend by nature, and the program asks it with `use java`, which the native
# backend refuses by design.
#
# run.sh still calls `__emitc` and fails if it succeeds, so this file cannot
# silence a program that does have a native half.
